11. Previous diagnosis of autoimmune disease or requiring long-term use of systemic corticosteroids (dose \>10 mg/day prednisone or equivalent) or other immunosuppressants within 4 weeks prior to the first dose of study drug; however, patients are allowed to be enrolled in the following conditions: in the absence of active autoimmune disease, inhaled or topical steroids, or adrenaline replacement therapy at the dose ≤10 mg/day Prednisone equivalent is allowed to be used;
